                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "fontface": 0,
                                    "fontname": "Lato",
                                    "fontsize": 10.0,
                                    "id": "obj-114",
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 820.0, 730.0, 111.0, 18.0 ],
                                    "text": "manuel@cycling74.com"
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "id": "obj-113",
                                    "linecount": 4,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 570.0, 130.0, 130.0, 64.0 ],
                                    "text": "(to spare patching space, parameters are described as hints in the top-level patcher)"
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "fontface": 0,
                                    "id": "obj-112",
                                    "linecount": 3,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 790.0, 530.0, 181.0, 50.0 ],
                                    "text": "Finally, all signals pass through a second level limiter and a Dry/Wet balance unit."
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "fontface": 0,
                                    "id": "obj-111",
                                    "linecount": 3,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 790.0, 480.0, 200.0, 50.0 ],
                                    "text": "The Volume~ subpatcher is a mixing console that allows you to adjust the levels of the different signals."
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "fontface": 0,
                                    "id": "obj-110",
                                    "linecount": 3,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 790.0, 430.0, 190.0, 50.0 ],
                                    "text": "In between, the pitched/chorused signals are sent to the output (Volume~) for direct monitoring."
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "fontface": 0,
                                    "id": "obj-109",
                                    "linecount": 4,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 790.0, 360.0, 191.0, 64.0 ],
                                    "text": "The transformed signals are then returned to the reverberator, after treatment to better manage adverse effects due to feedback."
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "fontface": 0,
                                    "id": "obj-104",
                                    "linecount": 11,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 790.0, 190.0, 180.0, 165.0 ],
                                    "text": "The signals then pass through a reverberator (Reverb~) which creates the overall room effect. Reverberant signals are sent to multiple units:\n- transpose effect one octave down (Octave~)\n- direct to output monitoring (Volume~)\n- cascading effects chain with pitch shifting, chorus and delay."
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "fontface": 1,
                                    "id": "obj-67",
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 790.0, 100.0, 70.0, 21.0 ],
                                    "text": "Description"
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "background": 1,
                                    "fontface": 0,
                                    "id": "obj-68",
                                    "linecount": 4,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 790.0, 120.0, 182.0, 64.0 ],
                                    "text": "Input signals first pass through a level limiter used to later control the level of feedback that will be re-injected into the loop."
                                }
                            },
